# Copy to backend/.env. Rules mode does not send any data to a model service.
AI_MODE=rules
# For a school/self-hosted Chat Completions-compatible server:
# AI_MODE=chat
# AI_BASE_URL=https://your-school-model.example/v1
# AI_MODEL=your-model-name
# AI_API_KEY=configure-locally-only
# For a pre-existing agent accepting the documented /review contract:
# AI_MODE=agent
# AI_BASE_URL=https://your-school-agent.example
# Only if the approved internal endpoint requires HTTP:
# AI_ALLOW_INTERNAL_HTTP=1
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:password@localhost/graduate
# FILE_ROOT=runtime/files
# COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Agent-first workflow: complete Agent report before institutional confirmation.
# REVIEW_WORKFLOW=agent

# Additive PDF → OCR → material organization → fixed rules → bundle endpoint.
# By default the pipeline reuses AI_BASE_URL / AI_MODEL / AI_API_KEY above;
# these separate names are optional when the material pipeline needs another model.
# MATERIAL_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://your-school-model.example/v1
# MATERIAL_MODEL_NAME=your-material-model
# MATERIAL_MODEL_API_KEY=configure-locally-only
# MATERIAL_PDFTOPPM_BIN=pdftoppm
# MATERIAL_TESSERACT_BIN=tesseract
# MATERIAL_OCR_LANG=chi_sim+eng
# MATERIAL_OCR_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180

# Teacher paper queries default to the school's dedicated Pi service.
# Configure the backend's actual trusted Pi URL and absolute shared grant directory.
TEACHER_AGENT_MODE=innoagent
# TEACHER_AGENT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3108
# TEACHER_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# TEACHER_AGENT_MAX_QUERIES=5
# TEACHER_AGENT_MAX_TOOL_RETRIES=2
# TEACHER_AGENT_MAX_TURN_RETRIES=1
# Run one backend API worker and one backend replica. Turn grants live in the
# backend process that issued them. Keep WEB_CONCURRENCY and --workers at 1.
# TEACHER_AGENT_GRANT_DIR=/var/run/innograd/teacher-query-grants
# Set the grant directory on BOTH services. Use a private directory (0700)
# owned by their shared service UID, outside all Pi workspaces. In containers,
# mount the same backing directory read-write on the backend and read-only on Pi.
# The filename is the exact Pi session filename, including .jsonl.
#
# On the dedicated Pi service, pin defaultProvider/defaultModel to the school
# deployment and provision only that provider's credentials. Use a private
# absolute TEACHER_PI_HOME and use it as HOME when launching this worker.
# In "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/config/config.json", set mcp.enabled to true, turn off
# memory.l1Enabled, memory.l2Enabled and memory.l3Enabled, and disable
# plugins.codemode, webAccess, todo, computerUse and permissionSystem.
# "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/config/settings.json":
# {"defaultTools":[],"extensions":["-builtin:mcp"]}
# "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/config/mcp-adapter.json":
# {"settings":{"allowInstall":false,"namespaceProxyTools":false,"outputGuard":false},"mcpServers":{}}
# The dedicated adapter retains the raw authorized result needed to verify
# each successful run ID. It does not spill large results to temporary files.
#
# Install backend/skills/teacher-query-planner under "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/skills".
# Copy its extensions/teacher-query-planner.ts to
# "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/config/extensions/teacher-query-planner.ts".
# In Pi's environment, set the backend's Streamable HTTP endpoint and the
# absolute entry path of the pi-mcp-adapter installed with its InnoAgent build.
# TEACHER_AGENT_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/teacher-agent/mcp
# Local example from the InnoGrad project root:
# export TEACHER_AGENT_MCP_ADAPTER="$(realpath ../inno-agent-audit-20261015/apps/inno-agent/node_modules/pi-mcp-adapter/index.ts)"
# TEACHER_PI_SERVER="$(realpath ../inno-agent-audit-20261015/apps/inno-agent/dist/server.js)"
# (cd "$TEACHER_PI_HOME" && env HOME="$TEACHER_PI_HOME" node "$TEACHER_PI_SERVER" --home "$TEACHER_PI_HOME" --config-dir "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/config" --skills-dir "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/skills" --data-dir "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/data" --workspace "$TEACHER_PI_HOME/workspace" --port 3108)
#
# Use a trusted TLS link when Pi and the backend are on separate hosts.
# The extension binds the MCP server to the current session's grant before
# the first model request. Keep Authorization headers out of logs. The
# backend unlinks the grant before deleting the isolated session and workspace.
# Explicit legacy modes are TEACHER_AGENT_MODE=rules and TEACHER_AGENT_MODE=chat.
